@startuml wallbreaker-scdawg-walk
' WallBreaker pipeline for large error bounds (k ≥ 5), complementing the
' pigeonhole-split diagram: split the query into k+1 pieces, locate each exact
' piece with the bidirectional SCDAWG, then extend & verify candidates.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #37474F
  LifeLineBorderColor #455A64
  ParticipantBorderColor #D84315
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFCCBC
  ParticipantFontColor #102027
}

title WallBreaker — split → locate (SCDAWG) → verify   (large error bound k <latex>\ge</latex> 5)

participant "WallBreakerQuery\nW · k" as Q #FFCCBC
participant "PatternSplitter" as S #FBE9E7
participant "SCDAWG\nbidirectional substring index" as D #C8E6C9
participant "Verifier\nexact distance <latex>\le</latex> k" as V #E1BEE7

Q -> S : split W into k+1 pieces
note over S #FBE9E7: pigeonhole principle —\nat least one piece is error-free
loop each piece <latex>p_{i}</latex>
  S -> D : locate exact occurrences of <latex>p_{i}</latex>
  D --> V : candidate terms containing <latex>p_{i}</latex>
  V -> V : extend left/right,\ncompute d(W, term)
end
V --> Q : terms with d(W, term) <latex>\le</latex> k
@enduml
